        ("What is a sample in statistics?", "A subset of individuals selected from a larger population", ["The entire population", "An error in data", "A formula"], "A sample is a representative subset drawn from a population to infer population parameters."),
        ("What is a parameter versus a statistic?", "Parameter describes a population; Statistic describes a sample", ["Parameter is sample; Statistic is population", "They are identical", "Parameter is always zero"], "Parameters (e.g., mu, sigma) describe populations; statistics (e.g., x-bar, s) describe samples."),
