        ("What is the Difference between Perfect Forward Secrecy (PFS) and non-PFS key exchanges in TLS?", "PFS uses ephemeral Diffie-Hellman keys so past session traffic cannot be decrypted if server private key leaks", ["PFS uses static keys forever", "PFS disables encryption", "PFS stores all keys in cloud"], "PFS generates unique session keys for every connection; compromising the long-term server key cannot decrypt past captures."),
        ("What is a Timing Attack in side-channel cryptography?", "Attacker infers secret keys by analyzing subtle differences in execution time of cryptographic operations", ["Clock frequency hacking", "Changing computer time zones", "Delaying network packets"], "Non-constant-time comparisons (e.g., memcmp on hashes) leak character matches via microscopic timing variations."),
        ("What is Certificate Transparency (CT) in modern web PKI?", "Publicly auditable, append-only cryptographic log of all issued SSL/TLS certificates", ["Browser history sharing", "Publishing private keys online", "Encrypting DNS queries"], "CT logs use Merkle trees to detect rogue, fraudulent, or misissued certificates for domains in real time."),
